{title: What A Wonderful World}
{artist: Louis Armstrong}
{key: F}

{c: Verse 1}
[F] [Am],        I see trees of green
[Dm] [Am],        Red roses too
[Gm] [F],        I see them bloom
[A] [Dm],        For me and you
[A#] [Gm],        And I think to myself
[C] [F],        What a wonderful world
[F] [Am],        I see skies of blue
[Dm] [Am],        And clouds of white
[Gm] [F],        The bright blessed day
[A] [Dm],        The dark sacred night
[A#] [Gm],        And I think to myself
[C] [F],        What a wonderful world
[C],        The colors of the rainbow
[F],        So pretty in the sky
[C],        Are also on the faces
[F],        Of people going by
[Dm] [Am],        I see friends shaking hands
[Dm] [Am],        Saying, "How do you do?"
[Dm] [Am],        Theyre really saying
[Gm] [C],        "I love you"
[F] [Am],        I hear babies cry
[Dm] [Am],        I watch them grow
[Gm] [F],        Theyll learn much more
[A] [Dm],        Than Ill never know
[A#] [Gm],        And I think to myself
[C] [F],        What a wonderful world
